course: dictionary
lesson: 6810
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word original has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one to use. Its first meaning is existing at the very start, before anything changed: «the original plan» is the first plan, before any changes were made.
explain: Its second meaning is new and not copied: «an original idea» is one you thought of yourself. «A cover is a song written by someone else; an original is one the band wrote itself.» Here original means the song the band made, not a copy of someone else's song.
explain: In maths, original means the amount before a change. If a price goes up or down, the original price is the one you start with. Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if «the first plan» still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Original means first, or existing at the beginning, before any changes.
fact: Original can also mean new and not copied, like «an original story».
fact: «The original» as a noun means the real thing, not a copy.
fact: In maths, «the original price» is the price before a change, such as a sale or a rise.
fact: «In its original form» means the form something had at the start.
exercise: «A cover is a song written by someone else; an original is one the band wrote itself.» What does original mean here? | Written by someone else | Sung in the past | Sung very loudly | *Written by the band itself, not copied
exercise: A bag costs £12, and then its price goes up to £15. What is the original price? | £15 | £3 | £27 | *£12
exercise: «Releases work only when the wild habitat is protected and the original danger is gone.» What does original danger mean? | Brand new danger that has just started | A danger someone copied from elsewhere | The safest place to play | *The danger that was there at the beginning
test: In the lesson's example «I couldn't care less» and «I could care less», which phrase is the original? | «I don't care at all» | Neither, because both are new | «I could care less» | *«I couldn't care less»
test: A museum keeps the original document, not a copy. What does the museum keep? | A copy made later | A new book about documents | A photo of a document | *The first real document
exam: «A quote can be checked in its original source.» What does original source mean? | The newest website about the quote | A copy that a friend made | A song the band wrote | *The first place the quote was written or said
